Agent in AI

An AI Agent is built on top of an LLM (like Gemini, GPT-4).

It has reasoning + autonomy + can use tools.

Purpose: perform cognitive tasks.

Example:

A Financial Advisor Agent that queries BigQuery + suggests portfolios.

A DevOps AI Agent that reads logs + suggests fixes.

Key Features:

Uses an LLM for reasoning.

Can call external APIs/tools (e.g., databases, shells, Slack, Jira).

Can maintain memory and perform multi-step tasks.

Focus: automation of knowledge work.

 Think of it as a smart worker that plans & acts.


