Agent in Azure (Self-Hosted Agent for DevOps Pipelines)

In Azure DevOps, an agent is a compute resource (VM, container, machine) that runs your CI/CD pipeline jobs.

Purpose: execute build/test/deploy tasks.

Example:

You run a pipeline in Azure DevOps → the self-hosted agent on your EC2 or VM runs the scripts (Terraform, Docker build, etc.).

Key Features:

Executes YAML pipeline steps (build, test, deploy).

Can be Microsoft-hosted (managed by Azure) or Self-hosted (your VM).

Focus: automation of software delivery.

💡 Think of it as a runner/worker machine for DevOps tasks.
